{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_vrtx_01Saybg1YLMeHJqMhadUioYd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. Here's what was written for **Q26 — Control cost explosions from tool calls**:\n\n---\n\n**Six control levers covered:**\n\n1. **Orchestrator hard limits** — `max_turns` (5–10), `max_tokens_per_task`, wall-clock timeout, and a per-task USD spend cap enforced in code, *never* in the prompt (the LLM will ignore prompt-level iteration instructions)\n\n2. **Context compression** — naive agents re-send the full tool-call history on every turn, causing quadratic token growth; fix with a sliding window (last 3 turns) or a cheap-model summarization step at turn 5+\n\n3. **Model tiering** — route tool-selection and summarization turns to GPT-4o-mini (~15× cheaper); escalate to GPT-4o only for synthesis steps via a LangGraph conditional edge\n\n4. **Tool-call caching + deduplication** — hash `(tool_name, args)` → Redis cache with TTL; use OpenAI parallel tool calls to batch multiple tool requests into one LLM turn\n\n5. **Narrow tool schemas** — purpose-built `get_order_status(order_id)` instead of `query_database(sql)` reduces argument tokens and hallucination retries\n\n6. **HITL gate for expensive branches** — gate multi-step expensive tool chains with cost estimates and human confirmation before launch\n\n**Cost math:** naive agent at 1M queries/day → $250K/day; tiered+cached+capped → $8K/day (30× reduction, mostly from model tiering and caching)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":393,"cache_read_input_tokens":68089,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":393,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8694a335-8310-4e20-9646-f7b767b5287f","uuid":"6a358435-f16c-4619-abdc-864774c54791"}
